  "diagnosis_status": "source_supported",
  "diagnosis_summary": "Public Rock 19.2 source uses a shared mutable Dictionary cache in the static AzureBlobStorageClient and performs a ContainsKey/Add sequence without visible synchronization. Microsoft documents that Dictionary requires caller synchronization when reads and writes can overlap. This supports a concurrency defect in the Azure-backed BinaryFile path, but it does not by itself prove that the reported 100 percent CPU incident or a specific call stack had this cause; the upstream issue remains open without a recorded fix.",
